{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:UGB.UnitalGroebner.s_polynomial_decomposition","@type":"LeanModule","name":"UGB.UnitalGroebner.s_polynomial_decomposition","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgOps"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.UnitalGroebner.s_polynomial_decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.UnitalGroebner.s_polynomial_decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/UnitalGroebner/s_polynomial_decomposition.lean#L44-L87","doc":"**S-polynomial decomposition — base (two-rule) case.**\n\nThe two rules `f₁, f₂` share a leading monomial `α` with unit leading\ncoefficients `a₁, a₂`; the combination `c₁f₁ + c₂f₂` cancels at `α`\n(`c₁a₁ + c₂a₂ = 0`, i.e. its leading monomial drops strictly below\n`α`). Then the combination is a scalar multiple of the S-polynomial.\n\nThe conclusion is a **concrete `AlgElement` equation** — the real\ncontent the former `holds : Prop` lacked. The expected witness is\n`d = c₁·a₁`. A complete proof needs coefficient extensionality for\n`AlgElement` (which is a raw data structure, not a quotient — see the\n`AlgOps.lean` §6 design note); supplying that ext principle is the\nremaining manuscript step. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:s-polynomial-decomposition","label":"prop:s-polynomial-decomposition","md":"unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/s-polynomial-decomposition.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.UnitalGroebner.sPolynomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.UnitalGroebner.sPolynomial","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/UnitalGroebner/s_polynomial_decomposition.lean#L37-L42","doc":"The **S-polynomial** about two rules with unit leading coefficients\n`a₁, a₂`:  `S(f₁,f₂) = a₁⁻¹ · f₁  −  a₂⁻¹ · f₂`, built from the\nconcrete `AlgElement` scalar-multiplication and subtraction\n(`AlgOps.lean`). A real construction, not an axiom. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:s-polynomial","label":"def:s-polynomial","md":"unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/s-polynomial.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}